title: 'M1.6 slice 2 reading: meter restore joins usage to permit.grant'
summary: budget.usage rows carry no loop, so the boot rebuild joins each usage row to its permit.grant on the chain and attributes along the permit's axes; a usage row with no grant counts nothing (never guessed). 'Today' and the 5 h window come from the chain's last event time (S-L2, new KernelLog.lastEventAt), never the wall clock, so replay reproduces them. Today's budget.ladder rows are restored so a rung is never said twice in a day. Permits are not restored (live per connection). quotaErrors stays a since-boot counter.
